# ── What is NOT compared, and why (K-629) ────────────────────────────────────
#
# SCAN_ROOTS leaves the Rails skeleton out. That was a decision, but it was never
# written down anywhere, so the next reader had to re-derive it from the absence
# of an entry — and "no entry" reads the same whether a path was considered and
# excluded or simply never noticed. These are the ~30 paths that exist in two or
# more demos and that nothing above compares (eight of the original set — the
# T-048 statics, the three error pages, puma.rb and the test/production envs —
# have since been PROMOTED into COPIES above: K-643). Each line says what the
# copies are allowed to differ by; measured, not assumed.
#
# HONEST SCOPE, twice over.
#
# (1) These entries are DOCUMENTARY. Only their staleness is checked (a declared
#     path that no longer exists in two demos is an error), not their
#     completeness: proving no OTHER skeleton path is duplicated would mean
#     walking the whole demo tree, which is full of gitignored local scratch
#     (log/, tmp/, .bundle/, node_modules/), and filtering that needs `git
#     ls-files` — an external process, in a check that deliberately runs on a
#     bare checkout with nothing but stdlib. The scan roots keep their
#     undeclared-copy guard; the skeleton has a record instead.
#
# (2) "Not compared" is not "not covered". config/routes.rb and
#     config/initializers/kiosk.rb ARE asserted, on the four telemetry-wiring
#     patterns at the bottom of this file; db/structure.sql is the output of
#     migrations this check compares byte-for-byte; and every demo's whole
#     skeleton is exercised by that demo's CI job, which boots the app.
#
# One recurring shape, stated once instead of forty times: kiosk-demo-prove is a
# smaller, API-only Rails app generated on its own, so on a whole family of
# generator-output paths the seven operator demos agree byte-for-byte and prove
# alone differs. Where a reason below says "prove differs", that is what it means.
